<title>USA: Ahmanson sets $250 mln stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Ahmanson sets $250 mln stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>IRWINDALE, Calif. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>H.F. Ahmanson &amp; Co., parent of Home Savings of America, on Wednesday said its board has authorized a new $250 million common stock buyback plan.</p>
<p>In a statment, the company said the new program is its fourth such plan. Including it, the company will have authorized the repurchase of $900 million worth of common stock and $175 million in preferred stock since October 1995.</p>
<p>Through March 31, Ahmanson acquired 19.2 million common shares, or 16 percent of the common stock outstanding before the first stock buyback. The share price averaged $27.11. At March 31, it had 100.6 million common shares outstanding.</p>
